WEBVTT

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.470
This is my last game.

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.930
Shiki, Joshua...

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.100
I'm going...

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.600
...to survive...

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.270
...these seven days!

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.650
There's the mission!

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.910
Reach 104. You have 60 minutes.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.320
The cost of failure is erasure.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.130
"The World Ends With You The Animation"

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:08.710
"#08: Emergency Call"

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:11.960
"#08: Emergency Call"
Hasn't the Reapers' Game
been weird lately?

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.670
It's just barely legal, perfectly
threading the loopholes in the rules.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:21.430
A dark grey area just shy of black.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:26.810
Anyway, a job's still a job.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:30.810
Yeah, but there's no way this will fly.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:33.860
With only one Player, it's not even a job.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.650
Ms. Konishi is the Game Master,

00:02:36.650 --> 00:02:40.410
and I won't get the chance
to show off for her!

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:43.330
Oh, the Iron Maiden?

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.670
Damn it!

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:54.090
I can't go anywhere like this!

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.420
I need to find a partner soon.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.140
"This game only has... one Player"?!

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.270
It's just me?!

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:09.350
I can't fight Noise without a partner!

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:15.020
What's my move?
Run away for seven days somehow?

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:19.490
As soon as a I get a mission to
beat Noise, I'm guaranteed to fail.

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:25.990
Found you!

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:27.330
Reapers!

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:36.090
Don't blame us. Just doing our jobs.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:38.920
I'll count down to your touching finale.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.050
Start!

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:44.600
Ten! Nine! Eight!

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:47.600
Seven! Six!

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.640
Oh, I'm sick of this!

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:51.350
Zero!

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.610
Wha--?!

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.650
Bye-bye now.

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:01.570
Damn it.

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:04.530
This can't... be the end.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:09.950
I'm holding back,
so put up more of a fight!

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.120
I won't lose!

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.840
Could this be the end?

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:21.220
Yo, yo, yo, not so fast!

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:27.390
Beat!

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.180
You're playing way too dirty!

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:32.180
Who invited you?!

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:35.060
Ah, youth.

00:04:35.060 --> 00:04:38.400
First, I get ordered to
take out my old buddies...

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:44.530
...and now there's only one
Player in this game?!

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:50.790
What gives?!

00:04:57.250 --> 00:05:02.380
The Composer might be cool
with this, but I sure ain't!

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:05.220
I'm gonna wipe the floor with you!

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.720
Don't tell me you're betraying us?

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:08.640
Sure am!

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.180
Think about it, though.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:13.680
It's obviously a losing battle.

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:16.650
Are you stupid?

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.730
You're the stupid ones!

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:19.980
Huh?

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.570
Yo, Phones.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.650
Huh?

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:28.450
We're making a pact this
time around. You got that?

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:29.660
Fine!

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.960
For now, let's run.

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.210
Yeah!

00:05:41.210 --> 00:05:42.050
Get back here--

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:45.670
Uzuki! Stop, stop!

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:50.470
We've got to report to the boss.
That's basic professionalism.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:54.560
Now, what kind of party have
they got in store for us?

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:01.150
Mission cleared.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:03.320
Thanks, you were a real life saver.

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:09.110
Didn't you used to be a lot less open?

00:06:09.110 --> 00:06:11.490
Why'd you make a pact with me?

00:06:12.530 --> 00:06:16.620
'Cause you were too pathetic, and the
Reapers were playing too dirty!

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:18.330
It hurt to watch!

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:22.460
Plus, you know,

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.920
I owed you for this.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:26.550
Rhyme's pendant?

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:32.050
It's no big deal. I just picked
it up and returned it.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:37.850
Plus, you're a Reaper. Won't partnering
with a Player get you in big trouble?

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:43.150
Oh, just quit whinin'!

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:46.110
The pact worked, so who cares?!

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:47.950
Hey...

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:48.780
Yeah?!

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:51.320
Your wings are gone!

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:53.330
Oh yeah, you're right.

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:55.080
Is that a problem?

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:59.790
Ha! I've had it with
the way they do things!

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:03.420
This is more my speed!

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.170
Wait, you were teamed up
with some prissy kid.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:10.800
What are you playing another game for?

00:07:10.800 --> 00:07:13.510
He--Joshua...

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.890
So, that's how it is.

00:07:17.890 --> 00:07:20.730
And you ended up with that shitty penalty.

00:07:20.730 --> 00:07:22.520
Yeah.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:29.030
I mean, lettin' a living Player in
was the Reapers' screwup, right?

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:31.360
Shades is such a piece of...

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:34.620
They've still got Shiki as my entry fee.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.500
I guess we've gotta win this thing.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:40.580
Yeah.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.580
OK, follow me!

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:45.290
Huh? Where to?

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:48.380
There's someplace we've gotta go up ahead.

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:49.420
Let's move!

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:51.260
Hey, wait up, Beat!

00:07:53.840 --> 00:07:58.100
Just watch! I'll take this
wall like, wham! Bang!

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:01.270
I've got no clue what you mean.

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:03.270
I got that from Rhyme a lot.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.690
That Noise...

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:09.070
This is Rhyme's soul.

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:13.200
Hanekoma picked up the pieces and
turned her into a Noise to save her.

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:19.410
I figured I could bring her
back if I turned Reaper,

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:23.210
but it turns out only the
Composer can do that stuff.

00:08:24.290 --> 00:08:28.090
Just between us, I'm gonna
become the Composer.

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:30.460
Can a human do that?

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:31.510
Yeah.

00:08:31.510 --> 00:08:35.470
Whoever takes down the
Composer becomes the next one.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:37.550
Hanekoma broke it down for me.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:41.730
Is there anything
Mr. Hanekoma <i>doesn't </i>know?

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:47.020
Don't worry! The Composer can
bring people back to life and stuff,

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:51.570
so once I'm in charge, I'll bring back
you and Shiki and everybody else!

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:55.990
I've got an idea where
the Composer might be.

00:08:57.160 --> 00:08:58.910
So do I.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:02.160
The Shibuya River.

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:06.330
Noise!

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:18.050
Open up, wall!

00:09:20.970 --> 00:09:23.520
All right!

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:25.690
Huh? How'd you do that?

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.610
With a Reaper keypin!

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:33.740
They have keys? That sounds handy.

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:38.700
'Course, it can only open
walls in the area I run.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:43.290
Only Reapers on Ironface's
level got keys to all of them.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.160
Who?

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:49.040
The Game Master this time.
Her name's Konishi.

00:09:50.250 --> 00:09:53.510
A Reaper has rebelled, sir.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.470
Daisukenojo Bito.

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:59.300
The newcomer you gave
a special assignment.

00:09:59.300 --> 00:10:03.350
He's been with us eight days.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:07.730
As Game Master, I will
address this issue personally.

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:11.610
No, we'll treat him as a Player.

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:14.900
I believe I'm currently the Game Master.

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:21.990
Are you talking back?
Will wonders never cease?

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:25.620
In order to erase Neku Sakuraba
and Daisukenojo Bito,

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:30.040
all Reapers will be required
to equip Outlet Pins.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:31.750
Are you sure, sir?

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:34.920
Do you want any more killed in action?

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:39.550
We're out of time.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:43.180
I'm putting the Underground
on Emergency Call.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:47.020
Emergency Call?!

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:51.100
The rest is up to you.
I trust you can handle it?

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:54.940
Yes, sir. I understand.

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:57.400
It's strange.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:00.610
Why so much alarm over mere Players?

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:09.370
I see I'll require more data to
accurately grasp the situation.

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:12.540
My plan demands hard facts.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:17.760
Reapers' Games three weeks in a row, huh?

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.760
Not exactly motivating.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:23.220
If you request a leave, I will approve it.

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:24.560
Huh?!

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:28.060
M-Ms. Konishi! I didn't
mean to suggest that...

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:31.060
Uzuki's looking for a challenge.
Isn't that right?

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:33.560
Th-That's right!

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:35.730
Then, I have special orders for you.

00:11:35.730 --> 00:11:37.030
We're honored!

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:40.820
You're a capable Reaper, Yashiro.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:43.870
If you get results,
your promotion is assured.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:47.620
Did you hear that, Kariya?!

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.080
I sure did.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.080
As for you, Mr. Kariya,

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:54.790
with your strength,
you should already be--

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:56.000
So...

00:11:57.210 --> 00:12:01.050
...what will you be doing, ma'am?

00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:04.340
Me? I'm going on the offensive.

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:07.100
From a place no one will find me.

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:11.190
"Shibuya Station Underpass"

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:16.520
Joshua was always looking
for the Composer.

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:20.990
He had his eye on Shibuya River, but he
couldn't get deep enough inside.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:21.950
Yeah.

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:27.280
I hear if you try to force your way in,
you end up Taboo Noise chow.

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:29.160
Is that how it works?

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:31.830
What's up?

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:38.500
How do you do?

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:40.050
Ironface!

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:44.050
I am the current Game Master,
Mitsuki Konishi.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:44.800
Daisuke--

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:49.970
That's "Beat" to you!

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:55.150
Despite having received special orders,

00:12:55.150 --> 00:13:00.070
you've been guarding Neku Sakuraba
against Noise under the guise of combat.

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:03.860
Busted, huh?

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:05.030
Even I realized that.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:07.160
Huh?!

00:13:07.160 --> 00:13:12.160
You deserve immediate erasure, but because
you've concluded a Partner Pact,

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:15.620
I've elected to treat you as a Player.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:19.500
What, you here to collect
my entry fee or somethin'?

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:22.260
Exactly. The thing you care for most is...

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.970
Not gonna happen!

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:32.430
Beat!

00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:49.070
Stop!

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:54.750
I will collect this Noise
as your entry fee.

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:58.290
If you want her returned,
complete your missions.

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:10.140
Give her back!

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:14.270
Give back Rhyme!

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:23.690
Rhyme!

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:30.240
I will now assign you your mission.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:34.620
Find and defeat me.

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:36.910
I'll take care of that right here!

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:38.540
Calm down!

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:41.250
You have six days.

00:14:41.250 --> 00:14:42.380
Six <i>days</i>?!

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:46.300
I will remain in a certain
place for six days.

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:50.470
If you don't want to be erased,
you must find me as soon as possible,

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:53.310
and clear your mission.

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:57.560
Calling all Reapers.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:04.320
In the name of the Game Master,
I declare an Emergency Call.

00:15:05.730 --> 00:15:09.860
Erase the rebel Beat on sight!

00:15:09.860 --> 00:15:14.160
Erase his partner Neku as well!

00:15:14.160 --> 00:15:17.910
Erase the rebel Beat on sight!

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:22.290
Erase his partner Neku as well!

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:24.090
Not good.

00:15:24.090 --> 00:15:25.380
Let's move!

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:33.260
An Emergency Call is one thing,

00:15:33.260 --> 00:15:36.310
but equipping O-Pins?

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:39.230
Secret weapons that boost our powers?

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:40.980
I can't wait!

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:46.860
Do you know why we haven't used
those secret weapons before now?

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:49.320
They put a lot of strain on us, right?

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:56.790
They look like the pins that
are all the rage in Shibuya.

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:59.540
Actually, aren't they the same?

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:01.670
Is this the Composer's style?

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:04.080
I can't believe we have to wear these.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:07.000
What's got the brass so nervous?

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:19.730
Shit!

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:25.310
Ironface ain't plannin'
on lettin' us find her!

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:27.770
Beat!

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:29.030
Thanks, Neku!

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:35.490
We won't last forever. Where is she?

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.160
There you are, traitor.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:43.000
I don't remember joinin' your team!

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:46.750
I'll take you on, but I'm
more than you can handle.

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:48.130
In your dreams!

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:51.010
We've got O-Pins.

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:53.510
Go!

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:10.150
Beat!

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:15.780
Damn!

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:19.200
We ain't got time for this right now!

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:20.660
Don't get careless!

00:17:20.660 --> 00:17:21.870
Same to you!

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:41.850
We'll kick all your asses!

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:43.810
Pretty much, yeah.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:50.770
Just you wait, Ironface!

00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:58.450
She ran in there, right?

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:00.200
O-East?

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.700
"Sold Out"
"All tickets for today's show have
been sold. Thank you for your interest."

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:06.870
We've been here before, right?

00:18:08.460 --> 00:18:12.500
It ain't even been two weeks since then.

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:16.970
Yeah, we were all together then.

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:20.260
You guys are back here?

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:23.310
You're...

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:27.900
Did you ever find your mic?

00:18:27.900 --> 00:18:29.400
Nah.

00:18:29.400 --> 00:18:31.940
Oh. I hope it turns up.

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:38.450
Tickets have been
selling like crazy lately.

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:39.740
Wow.

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:40.950
Right?

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:43.790
Go get ready for your show, then.

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:47.410
We ain't got time to waste on you.

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.630
We're looking for Konishi.

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:52.670
Ms. Konishi? I haven't seen her.

00:18:52.670 --> 00:18:55.380
I was sure she went in here.

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:56.970
Let's go.

00:18:58.590 --> 00:19:01.430
There's an Emergency Call on.

00:19:01.430 --> 00:19:04.100
Don't get in our way.

00:19:04.100 --> 00:19:09.060
I like my double life in the
Underground and Realground.

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:11.940
I don't know what you did
to make their hit list,

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:14.650
but I'll keep the peace
in the Underground.

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:16.570
I'm the bad guy now?!

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:20.410
Get ready, Daisukenojo Bito!

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:22.030
Dai... What?

00:19:22.030 --> 00:19:25.870
Don't call me that!

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:27.450
<i>That's </i>your name?

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:29.410
It's seriously uncool!

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:32.040
Only ever call me "Beat," got that?!

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:33.250
S-Sure.

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:37.090
Let's go, Daisukenojo Bito!

00:19:45.310 --> 00:19:46.680
Let's make this count!

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:47.890
You got it!

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:08.040
Have another one for free!

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:09.500
Get lost!

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:20.720
And that's that!

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:26.890
You're tough.

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:28.140
'Course we are!

00:20:28.140 --> 00:20:31.480
If you've learned your lesson,
start callin' me <i>Mr. </i>Beat.

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:32.560
Hey.

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:35.400
That wasted time. Let's get going!

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.650
Wait! I can still...

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:40.990
You've got a show today.

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:43.450
Aren't your fans and bandmates waiting?

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:47.410
My bandmates?

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:54.460
Take this.

00:20:54.460 --> 00:20:55.670
What is it?

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:58.050
My keypin.

00:20:58.050 --> 00:21:01.630
It'll open more walls than Beat's will.

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:05.340
You're sure?

00:21:05.340 --> 00:21:08.430
I don't like to owe people.

00:21:08.430 --> 00:21:11.390
Got it. Thanks, man!

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:14.900
I'll be in trouble if this
gets out. Get moving.

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:23.200
How am I supposed to put on a
show now you guys are gone?

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:32.660
I see you held back.

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:36.210
Ms. Konishi. How did you...?

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:39.250
I know I ordered you to
equip your Outlet Pin.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.920
Why did you fight without it?

00:21:43.050 --> 00:21:45.010
It wouldn't be fair.

00:21:46.890 --> 00:21:49.220
This is no time for this crap!

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:53.770
Reapers--my friends--are getting
killed by Taboo Noise!

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:56.400
Doesn't that take priority?

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:58.980
What are the bosses thinking?!

00:22:00.820 --> 00:22:03.070
If you can't obey orders...

00:23:44.420 --> 00:23:46.760
Next time: "Rhyme and Beat."
